WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:22.000
The filter, map, reduce pipeline
Array methods split a problem into stages. filter decides which items to keep, map transforms each item and reduce accumulates one result.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:44.000
Explanation
First select prices of at least 1000, then discount each by 10%, then sum them starting at 0. Write the intermediate array after each stage.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:01:06.000
Trace the code
const prices = [500, 1000, 2000];
const total = prices
  .filter(price => price >= 1000)
  .map(price => price * 0.9)
  .reduce((sum, price) => sum + price, 0);
console.log(total);

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:28.000
Result
2700

[1000, 2000] → [900, 1800] → 2700.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:50.000
Remember
filter and map return new arrays. An initial reduce value gives a defined result even when the array is empty.
